## Included content<a id="content"></a>

|     Module     | Purpose |
| -------------- | ------- |
| `fixture`      | Update an existing object through lifecycle hooks |
| `fixture_info` | Read public state through the command line |
| `fixture_plan` | Predict a declaration with real reads and no writer |

Use this variant for products whose supported administration interface is a
command line on the managed host. The fixture demonstrates an existing-only
resource. Products that create or delete need fixtures and contract cases for
those operations before shipping them.

## Execution and prerequisites<a id="execution-prerequisites"></a>

Ansible runs the modules on the managed host, or on an authorized delegate. The
caller supplies the installed product, credential, interpreter and trusted
locator. The fixture needs Python 3.9+, GNU `timeout`, `/usr/bin/env`, and a
seeded private directory. The `custom` locator accepts one absolute program path
under the declared Python interpreter. It verifies the numeric module UID and
probes the application UID through the same prefix before writing. Use `become`
to establish the user.

Commands stay in the foreground and run under one shared deadline, including
reads and identity probes. The locator clears the application's environment with
`env -i`, fixes its locale and rejects inherited loader overrides. It supports
neither container entry nor a user-switching wrapper. Product-specific locators
need their own qualification of identity, environment, deadline and cleanup.

